## Summary of "Copy Url" / Share URL Code in the SkyTube Project

I've completed a thorough analysis of the Android project (SkyTube, a NewPipe-like YouTube client) and found all the code that handles "Copy Url" / share URL functionality for videos, channels, and streams. Here are the key findings:

### Core URL Copying Implementation

**1. Main Copy URL Utility**
- **File**: `/Volumes/Dumpy/Research/automated_program_repair_for_ui_bugs/runs/claude_original_run1/bug-1255/app/src/main/java/free/rm/skytube/app/SkyTubeApp.java`
  - **Lines 423-427**: `copyUrl()` method that handles clipboard operations
  - **Lines 416-421**: `shareUrl()` method that creates share intents

```java
public static void copyUrl(@NonNull Context context, String text, String url) {
    ClipData clip = ClipData.newPlainText(text, url);
    ContextCompat.getSystemService(context, ClipboardManager.class).setPrimaryClip(clip);
    Toast.makeText(context, R.string.url_copied_to_clipboard, Toast.LENGTH_SHORT).show();
}

public static void shareUrl(@NonNull Context context, String url) {
    Intent intent = new Intent(android.content.Intent.ACTION_SEND);
    intent.setType("text/plain");
    intent.putExtra(android.content.Intent.EXTRA_TEXT, url);
    context.startActivity(Intent.createChooser(intent, context.getString(R.string.share_via)));
}
```

